# Non-secret runtime config for the fighter-edge-app project. Firebase loads
# this file on deploy. Secrets (the OpenRouter key) never go here — they live
# in Secret Manager.
#
# A chain, not one model, and in this order by measured latency on the real
# Fighter Brief prompt (2026-09-20): ~2-4s, ~3-4s, ~5-10s. All three passed
# 3/3 through the prompt and validator.
#
# Why a chain: on 2026-09-20 the free tier of the model this deployment had
# been using was withdrawn mid-day and every request came back 404, while
# other free models were intermittently 429 from their provider's shared
# pool. The function now walks this list on 404/429/5xx, so one model dying
# is no longer an outage. Free models are fine for a beta and are not
# contracts — expect to revisit this line.
#
# Delete this line to fall back to the paid DEFAULT_MODEL in
# src/openrouter.ts once the OpenRouter account is funded.
OPENROUTER_MODELS=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free,dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free,nex-agi/nex-n2.5-pro:free

# App Check (audit S-4). The app sends App Check tokens; the server refuses
# AI and billing-sync calls without one only when this is true. Switch it on
# after registering the apps in Firebase App Check and checking its metrics
# (docs/OWNER_SETUP.md, section 4).
ENFORCE_APP_CHECK=false

# Set to "deny" together with a paid model: OpenRouter then routes only to
# providers that don't store or train on prompts (audit S-5). Most free models
# have no such provider, so leave it unset while the chain above is free.
# OPENROUTER_DATA_COLLECTION=deny
